# ---- Downloaded empirical datasets (NOT committed) ----
# Large third-party downloads fetched on demand by generate_empirical_inputs.py
# (HYDE ~5.3 GB, ETOPO ~395 MB, raw zips, derived .npy, etc.). They exceed
# GitHub's file-size limit, are fully regenerable from the documented sources,
# and are optional at runtime (the empirical tests skip when absent). Regenerate
# with: python generate_empirical_inputs.py --<dataset>
data/empirical/

# NOTE: the rest of data/ (Natural Earth + precomputed earth_*.npy / present_day_*
# / landmask) IS committed on purpose so the app runs after a clone. See
# docs/data_attributions.md. To regenerate instead, delete those files and run
# the generate_*.py scripts.
